# Cells reading at the readout circuit's ceiling. A clipped cell reports the
# ceiling, not the pressure on it, so every frame it is clipped is data that
# cannot be recovered afterwards -- this says so while there is still time to
# unload the sensor or change the feedback resistor.
#
# 1050 suits Rfb = 8.2 kOhm, whose ceiling is about 1110 uS. Set it a little
# under your own circuit's ceiling.
app sat_watch {
  name    "Saturation Watch"
  version 1.0.0
  author  wenzi7777
  summary "Flags cells reading at the readout ceiling while it happens."
  category research
  icon    alert
}

signal clipped = active(1050)
event clipping when clipped > 0.5 for 50ms
signal episodes = counter(clipping)

# Reported when an episode ends: how many cells it reached, and how long.
signal worst = peak_since(clipped, clipping)
signal length = peak_since(duration(clipping), clipping)
emit clip_cells value worst on fall(clipping)
emit clip_ms value length on fall(clipping)

led red when clipping
pixel 8 red when clipping

show 0 "Clipped" clipped
show 1 "Peak" peak()
show 2 "Episodes" episodes
